# Planner consumer #1 — bare-param mutation through a MATCH GUARD (`case p if
# shrink(&xs):`). The guard lowers inside the arm's save/restore; the drift-free
# scope collector folds guards into the pre-scrutinee hoist set, so the param is
# materialized before the guard runs. Guard mutates via `&xs` (a mut-borrow
# callee), arm prints 99. Match guards are OUT of the ggdef phase-0 subset, so
# this lives in known_gaps/ and is validated on the two production backends only:
# C=99,3,4 and LLVM=99,3,4 (pre-fix both printed 99,4,4). SH note: mirrored on
# the self-host via the SMatch pre-scrutinee hoist.
bool shrink(Vector[int] &v):
    v.pop()
    return true

void f(Vector[int] xs):
    match xs.len():
        case 4 if shrink(&xs):
            print(99)
        else:
            print(88)
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
